{"seconds": 92.4, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! White is up a rook. This is the clearly winning line.\n\n**Summary:**\n- Best move: **Rb4+**\n- Main line: 1. Rb4+ Kg5 2. b6 (and Black's rook is trapped - if Rxb6, Rxb6 wins; if Rc8+, Kb7 and then Rb8+ Kxb8 wins)\n- Motif: **trappedPiece** (the Black rook on b8 has no escape)\n- The idea is to drive the king away with check, then advance the passed pawn, and the rook is trapped and will be captured.\n\n<coaching_note>\nWhen your opponent's piece is trapped with no escape squares, look for forcing moves (checks, captures) to drive away defenders or create threats. Here, Rb4+ forces the king away from protecting the rook, then b6 traps the Black rook on b8 permanently\u2014it must either be captured immediately (Rxb6 Rxb6) or it gets mated after the pawn advances. Always scan for trapped pieces in the enemy position.\n</coaching_note>\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rb4+\", \"line\": [\"Rb4+\", \"Kg5\", \"b6\", \"Rc8+\", \"Kb7\", \"Rb8+\"], \"motifs\": [\"trappedPiece\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42", "square": "b8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42", "square": "b3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42", "move": "Rb4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42", "move": "Rg3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r6/5p2/2K5/1P5p/6k1/1R6/1P6/8 w - - 8 42", "move": "b6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspec